		{
			"id": "E6VPO9G5sRLeAz2qf",
			"description": "Guardsman's Kit",
			"local_notes": "The standard web-gear/pack loadout carried by an Astra Militarum trooper on campaign.\n\nLore: The contents below are drawn from how Guard kit is consistently depicted across Black Library fiction (the Gaunt's Ghosts and Ciaphas Cain series in particular) and Astra Militarum background: unglamorous, faith-adjacent, and built around long marches and worse rations.\n\nDesign: A container grouping the small items below into one carried loadout, rather than tracking each separately; total weight/cost is the sum of the parts.",
			"tags": [
				"Gear",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_value": "60",
			"base_weight": "20 lb",
			"quantity": 1,
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "eIoy64wvkg0n7CN3Z",
					"description": "Uplifting Primer",
					"local_notes": "The Munitorum-issue catechism and basic-literacy primer given to every Guardsman; also a minor icon of faith.\n\nLore: A recurring, near-universal detail of Guard life in Black Library fiction — often quoted, occasionally mocked by veterans, carried by nearly everyone regardless.\n\nDesign: Flavour item; no mechanical effect.",
					"base_value": "5",
					"base_weight": "1 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "e3skWTgV-3QrMCNXQ",
					"description": "Lho-sticks (pack)",
					"local_notes": "A pack of rolled lho-leaf cigarettes, the Guard's ubiquitous off-duty vice.\n\nLore: Referenced constantly in Guard-focused fiction as shared currency, a nerve-settler before battle, and a habit officers alternately tolerate and ban.\n\nDesign: Flavour item; no mechanical effect.",
					"base_value": "10",
					"base_weight": "0.25 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eOf86nRhdQrs6tA8g",
					"description": "Ration Packs (week's supply)",
					"local_notes": "Preserved, nutritionally complete but famously unpleasant field rations.\n\nLore: A running joke and occasional plot point across Guard fiction, where rations are barely tolerable and traded for anything better.\n\nDesign: Standard GURPS travel rations (Basic Set) by another name, priced accordingly.",
					"base_value": "15",
					"base_weight": "10 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "ej9DXcV1WorowSVot",
					"description": "Bedroll",
					"local_notes": "Standard-issue sleeping roll.\n\nLore: Unremarkable but universal Guard kit.\n\nDesign: Flavour item; no mechanical effect.",
					"base_value": "15",
					"base_weight": "4 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eoslSb65lr13OB3gk",
					"description": "Mess Kit & Canteen",
					"local_notes": "Collapsible mess tin, utensils and a water canteen.\n\nLore: Standard Guard kit, occasionally a plot detail when water runs short.\n\nDesign: Flavour item; no mechanical effect.",
					"base_value": "10",
					"base_weight": "2 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "e52JkX4rLgCOW6C-R",
					"description": "Entrenching Tool",
					"local_notes": "Folding spade for digging in; usable in a pinch as an improvised weapon (treat as a small axe/shovel, sw-1 cut or thr cr).\n\nLore: A staple of trench-warfare-flavoured Guard depictions.\n\nDesign: Standard GURPS entrenching tool (Basic Set); the improvised-weapon note is a reasoned estimate, not a formal weapon anchor.",
					"base_value": "10",
					"base_weight": "2.5 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				},
				{
					"id": "eW96ljYMQ9Pl9Z1Ul",
					"description": "Aquila Icon",
					"local_notes": "A small icon of the Imperial faith worn or carried by most Guardsmen.\n\nLore: Nearly universal across Imperial citizenry, referenced throughout Black Library fiction regardless of a character's actual devoutness.\n\nDesign: Flavour item; no mechanical effect.",
					"base_value": "5",
					"base_weight": "0.25 lb",
					"quantity": 1,
					"equipped": true
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "eORlTmRoDBQB2Xo6L",
			"description": "Chrono",
			"local_notes": "A rugged wrist or pocket chronometer.\n\nLore: Unremarkable but near-universal personal timekeeping across the Imperium, mentioned in passing across Black Library fiction rather than dwelt on.\n\nDesign: No anchor; a plain GURPS wristwatch (Basic Set) equivalent, at a low TL since timekeeping is mechanically trivial regardless of setting.",
			"tags": [
				"Gear",
				"Imperium",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_value": "40",
			"base_weight": "0.25 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eKIzuPKgCuZMuKz9I",
			"description": "Glow-globe / Stablight",
			"local_notes": "Handheld or hung electric light; the glow-globe is a softer, room-lighting sphere, the stablight a focused beam torch.\n\nLore: Standard Imperial lighting, mentioned throughout Black Library fiction wherever characters move through unlit corridors, hab-blocks or underhive tunnels.\n\nDesign: No anchor; a plain GURPS flashlight/lantern (Basic Set) under Imperial naming, at a low TL since it's mechanically simple household/field tech.",
			"tags": [
				"Gear",
				"Imperium",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_value": "25",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "ecD4jMeCwMKaKklZz",
			"description": "Cameleoline Cloak",
			"local_notes": "A light-bending, pattern-disrupting cloak fabric; the bonuses above apply while the cloak is worn and the wearer is stationary or moving slowly enough to keep it effective (GM's call on faster movement).\n\nLore: Cameleoline cloaks are the signature camouflage gear of Imperial snipers and scout troops (Catachan and Tanith patterns both appear in Black Library fiction, most notably the Tanith First-and-Only's scouts in the Gaunt's Ghosts series) — a fabric that bends light and breaks up a wearer's outline rather than simple colour-matched cloth.\n\nDesign: No anchor; modelled as flat Stealth/Camouflage skill bonuses (a common GURPS convention for camouflage gear in Basic Set/Ultra-Tech-style items, applied here as an independently-reasoned value rather than copied from a specific catalogue entry) with no DR, since the cloak's whole function is concealment rather than protection. Restricted to LC2 to reflect its status as specialist rather than universal-issue kit.",
			"tags": [
				"Gear",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "8",
			"legality_class": "2",
